# data/users.json — INTENTIONALLY TRACKED despite being listed here.
# (v10.501 Phase 2 Arc C Batch 4c — closes GAP-002 via Path B
# accept-and-document.)
#
# The file is currently tracked in git history. It contains bcrypt
# password hashes (post-v10.497) and envelope-wrapped hashes
# (post-v10.500 Batch 3c), NOT plaintext. The previous comment here
# called the contents "plaintext credentials — replaced by hashed
# users in v10.497"; that wording was misleading on two counts
# (the file is now bcrypt-backed, AND it remained tracked despite
# the apparent gitignore entry).
#
# Why this entry exists at all:
#   - If the file is ever removed from the working tree (e.g. on a
#     fresh clone where the operator bootstraps from scratch), this
#     entry prevents it from being silently re-added by `git add .`
#     before the operator decides whether to bootstrap from a
#     generator or restore from a secure source.
#
# Why it's still tracked:
#   - Bootstrap-from-generator workflow (Path A) requires a
#     `generate_staff_v2.py` first-run prerequisite documented in
#     README + a separate sync mechanism for the operator's existing
#     user records. That work hasn't been designed.
#   - Path B (this batch) accepts current behaviour, documents the
#     inconsistency, and defers Path A to a future arc gated on
#     repo privacy posture changes.
#
# Operational discipline (codified in OPERATIONAL_PROTOCOL.md
# "Intentionally-tracked credential data"): do NOT run
# `git rm --cached data/users.json` to "fix" the apparent
# inconsistency. The tracking is intentional. If you genuinely want
# to switch to Path A, that becomes its own arc with a designed
# bootstrap-from-generator workflow.
data/users.json
# Versioned in-repo backup snapshots (use git history instead)
data/_v*_backups/
# Stale nested project copy (pre-v10.22, removed in cleanup before v10.497)
a2z/

# Auth-testing artifacts (cookie jars from curl/browser auth tests)
cookies.txt

# JWT revocation runtime state (per-session blocklist, not source)
data/jwt_blocklist.json

# ── Runtime mutation files (Batch 3d) ───────────────────────────────────
# These get rewritten on every request — they shouldn't have been tracked
# in the first place. New clones will not have them; the running app
# creates them on first audit-emitting action. To stop tracking the
# already-tracked copies, run:
#
#     git rm --cached data/audit_log.json
#     git rm --cached data/audit_trail.jsonl
#     git commit -m "Untrack runtime audit files (Batch 3d cleanup)"
#
# This is mentioned in docs/CHANGELOG_v10500_batch3d.md as a follow-up
# step the operator can run on their own schedule.
data/audit_log.json
data/audit_trail.jsonl

# ── Hotfix and migration backups (Batch 3d) ─────────────────────────────
# Per OPERATIONAL_PROTOCOL.md backup-before-mutation discipline. These
# files contain sensitive credential material (hashes, sometimes plain
# text during diagnostic sessions) and must never reach git or origin.
data/users.json.pre_*
data/users.json.post_*_migration
data/users.json.batch3c_tmp
*.pre_batch*_hotfix
utils/*.pre_*
utils/*.preBatch*
frontend_inspection.zip
frontend_inspection.zip
TEST_LOGINS.md
a2z/a2z/


# ── Hygiene: class-level backup / patcher / artifact ignores ────────────
# Catches the WHOLE class of throwaway files regardless of the specific
# suffix a script invents, so `git add -A` can't sweep them in.

# Any "before-mutation" snapshot, anywhere (covers .pre_<name>, .pre-<name>,
# .pre_<name>.json, *.pre_<name> etc.)
*.pre_*
*.pre-*
*.preBatch*

# Timestamped .bak snapshots (.bak-YYYY..., .bak_YYYY...)
*.bak-*
*.bak_*
*.bak

# Corruption/diagnostic auto-saves (the users.json.corrupt-* family)
*.corrupt-*
*.corrupt_*

# Reset / backup snapshot folders
data/_backups/
data/_reset_backup_*/

# Delivered patch kits land here as scripts/apply_*.py + README_*.md.
# Ignore the delivery artifacts (the real change is the patched source file,
# which you stage explicitly — never the patcher).
scripts/apply_*.py
scripts/diag_*.py
scripts/http_source_probe.py
scripts/storage_readiness_probe.py
README_*.md
_*_payload/
*.zip
run_*_probe.bat

# Misc local scratch
installed_packages.txt
.api
simulate_credit_chain (*).py

# credit document uploads (customer files — never commit)
data/uploads/credit_docs/
